- op: discuss  # 1ecb
  at: '2026-09-06T20:06:09Z'  # 1ecb
  by: agent  # 1ecb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1ecb
  clock: 9  # 1ecb
  nonce: 1ecb  # 1ecb
  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-09-06 (walk-through item 4): re-scope ACCEPTED as recommended. INV-hosig FOLDED into INV-bikaj as its named instance (duplicate_of link; invariants have no wont_do, so its status stays as filed and it leaves `ready`); INV-hujog stays the prerequisite; umbrella re-titled to the mechanism; P2 -> P3 (owner-authorised: it moves no analysis result, 4.5% of pass time on the 8-repo cohort). The mechanism (INV-hujog -> INV-bikaj) is appended to the END of the arc tail."  # 1ecb
- op: discuss  # 03cd
  at: '2026-09-16T19:27:55Z'  # 03cd
  by: agent  # 03cd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 03cd
  clock: 10  # 03cd
  nonce: 03cd  # 03cd
  message: "RE-VERIFIED AT TIP 2026-09-16 (dev db846f196f). BOTH HALVES OF THIS UMBRELLA'S\nSTATEMENT NOW HAVE A PRECISE ANSWER, AND ONE OF THEM IS THAT THE MECHANISM THIS\nITEM ASKS FOR ALREADY EXISTED WHEN THE ITEM WAS FILED.\n\nHALF (a), THE ACTIVATION PREDICATE. The statement asks that \"passes should\nconsult an activation predicate (analogous to a\nshould_run(detected_frameworks, detected_languages) check) and short-circuit\nwhen their target patterns are absent.\"\n\nThat predicate exists, with that name and that exact signature:\nLinkerActivation.should_run(detected_frameworks: set[str],\ndetected_languages: set[str]) -> bool, in linkers/registry.py, per ADR-3aaa.\nIt is ENFORCED, not decorative: run_all_linkers filters to active_linkers via\nlinker.activation.should_run(...) before dispatch. `git log -S` dates both the\nclass and the gating call to 55296f5440, 2026-01-30 (\"feat: implement ADR-0010\nmodular packages\") -- FOUR MONTHS BEFORE this item was filed on 2026-05-30. The\numbrella was filed against a mechanism already shipped and already wired.\n\nWHAT THE UMBRELLA ACTUALLY OWNS, therefore, is not \"build the gate\" but the\nDEFAULT. Census at tip, by AST over every register_linker call, 61 linkers:\n    24  genuinely gated (frameworks=... / language_pairs=...)\n    12  explicit activation=LinkerActivation(always=True) -- a deliberate,\n        readable \"this is a protocol linker, it always runs\"\n    25  NO activation= argument at all -> register_linker defaults to\n        LinkerActivation(always=True)\nSo 37 of 61 run unconditionally and 25 of those never said so. The permissive\nvalue is the DEFAULT, which makes \"nobody decided\" indistinguishable from \"we\ndecided it always runs\" -- the absent-versus-empty shape again, at the\nregistration site. All three linkers in WI-finij's silent cohort\n(graphql-resolver, message-queue, ipc) are in the defaulted 25.\ndi-resolution-linker (INV-hosig) is in the explicit 12.\n\nCOST, so the gate question is decidable rather than rhetorical. Post-fix\nself-survey at tip, 97 runs / 207647 ms pass time: the passes that read files\nand emitted nothing total 9922 ms = 4.78% of pass time, across 11 runs.\nNOT PERFORMED, DELIBERATELY: tightening an activation gate is the WITHHOLDING\ndirection. If framework detection misses, the linker does not run and real edges\ndisappear with no diagnostic. Trading recall for 4.78% of pass time is an owner\ndecision and wants bakeoff validation, so it is surfaced here with the numbers\nrather than shipped.\n\nHALF (b), THE RECORDED REASON. Shipped (silence_reason, INV-bikaj), and this\nsession found it was producing a FALSE reason. derive_silence_reason reads\nfiles_analyzed == 0 as the positive claim \"received zero input files\", but 0 is\nalso the dataclass default: EIGHT linkers read 14 to 834 files apiece, reported\n0, and were stamped no_candidate_files -- including di-resolution, this\numbrella's own named instance. Fixed in PR #1005 by deriving the count at the\nlinker chokepoint, with a gate against reintroduction. Distribution at tip moved\nno_candidate_files 51 -> 43, unreported 3 -> 11. Detail on WI-finij / INV-hosig.\nStill open on this half: 5 of the 7 declared silence values have NO producer,\nand 3 of those have free-text twins already in limits.skipped_passes (one\nconcept, two channels) -- WI-finij.\n\nMEMBER STATE, opened individually rather than inferred from each other:\n  INV-babuj  satisfied\n  INV-kodan  satisfied\n  INV-bikaj  SATISFIED 2026-09-16 (instrumentation shipped); residual WI-finij\n  INV-hosig  violated, folded into INV-bikaj; root_cause corrected today\n  INV-hujog  violated, owner-deferred -- and its re-open trigger CANNOT FIRE\n             (prerequisite_absent has no producer); recorded on that item\nStatus unchanged (violated)."  # 03cd
- op: discuss  # 8afd
  at: '2026-09-16T20:57:51Z'  # 8afd
  by: agent  # 8afd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8afd
  clock: 11  # 8afd
  nonce: 8afd  # 8afd
  message: "THE DEFAULT IS NOW DECLARED (PR #1007, dev 3e87d47890). Owner approved the\ndeclaration-only half; the gating half is untouched and this stays violated.\n\nWHAT THE 2026-09-16 ENTRY ABOVE IDENTIFIED AS WHAT THIS UMBRELLA ACTUALLY OWNS\n-- not \"build the gate\" (shipped 2026-01-30) but THE DEFAULT -- is fixed.\nregister_linker ended in:\n\n    activation=activation or LinkerActivation(always=True)\n\nso \"I considered gating and chose always-on\" and \"I never thought about it\"\nwere the same bytes. The 25 now declare always_on_unreviewed(), a factory\nbehaviourally identical to LinkerActivation(always=True) that claims a\ndifferent thing about the AUTHOR: runs unconditionally, and that is a default\nnobody defended.\n\nWHY NOT JUST WRITE LinkerActivation(always=True) ON ALL 25. That would have\nmanufactured 25 rationales nobody verified -- several of the 25 are Framework-\nsubcategory linkers (django-orm, jackson, kafka-streams, caddy-module,\nairflow, rust-trait, graphql-resolver) for which \"protocol linker, always\nruns\" would be an invented justification. It is the fabricated-disclosure\nfailure pass_silence already names: a reason invented on the producer's behalf\nis worse than no reason. The factory also makes the cohort greppable, which is\nwhat turns the gating question into a worklist:\n\n    grep -rl always_on_unreviewed packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/\n\nCENSUS RE-VERIFIED AT TIP, and it agrees exactly with the 2026-09-16 entry:\n61 registered / 24 gated / 12 deliberate always=True / 25 now-declared-unreviewed.\n\nBEHAVIOUR UNCHANGED, MEASURED NOT REASONED. The resolved activation map\n(always / frameworks / language_pairs) for all 61 linkers is byte-identical to\nthe pre-change tree, compared across a detached worktree with the loaded module\npath asserted -- an editable install otherwise resolves both runs to the same\ntree and reports a flattering IDENTICAL -- and with an injected mutation\nproving the comparison can report a difference at all.\n\nMY OWN INSTRUMENT WAS WRONG FIRST. Probe v1 filtered out modules starting with\n\"_\" and so never imported _third_party_bases.py, comparing 60 linkers in a\ncheck whose whole job was completeness. Caught only because 60 disagreed with\nthis item's own AST census of 61. One-of-N again, and the thing that caught it\nwas an implausible count, not an error.\n\nREGRESSION GATE: tests/test_linker_activation_declaration.py fails on any\nregister_linker in linkers/ that omits activation=, with a synthetic positive\ncontrol. AST-based, because the two @register_linker( in registry.py sit inside\ndocstring examples and a line pattern would count them as registrations --\nunfailable for the wrong reason from the day it was written. Ad-hoc\nregistrations inside test modules keep the default deliberately: a test pinning\npriority ordering has no opinion about activation.\n\nWHAT THIS ITEM STILL OWNS, AND WHY IT IS NOT MINE TO TAKE. Narrowing any of the\n25. Tightening an activation gate is the RECALL-LOSS direction: a missed\nframework detection silently drops real edges and leaves no hole where a hole\nwould be visible. The 2026-09-06 re-measure sized the prize at roughly one\ntwentieth of pass time on the 8-repo cohort; that is a cost saving paid for\nwith a correctness risk, so each of the 25 is a separate, evidence-backed,\nper-linker decision needing owner authorisation and bakeoff validation, not a\nsweep. Status stays violated."  # 8afd
- op: discuss  # 5c15
  at: '2026-09-17T01:06:06Z'  # 5c15
  by: agent  # 5c15
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5c15
  clock: 12  # 5c15
  nonce: 5c15  # 5c15
  message: "TIGHTENING REFUSED — ADR-0055, on measurement, not as a default. Status stays\nviolated: half (a) of this item's statement remains unmet BY DECISION now, with\nthe reasoning written down rather than left as a standing hesitation.\n\nTHE NUMBER THIS ITEM HAS BEEN CARRYING IS WRONG, AND THE INSTRUMENT WAS MINE.\nnanon_passes_09062026/readback.py filters silence as `edges_emitted == 0`,\nIGNORING nodes_emitted. pass_silence.py is explicit that a pass emitting nodes\nbut no edges is NOT silent, and that calling such passes silent \"would have been\nthe headline's original error repeated one level down\". apollo-server's\ngraphql-resolver-linker emitted 91 nodes and 0 edges and was counted as silent.\n\nRecomputed strictly (nodes==0 AND edges==0 AND files>0) over the same 9 cohort\nsurveys, total pass time 2,538,624 ms:\n\n  loose filter (the circulated 4.5%)            39,048 ms   1.54%\n  strict silence, all passes                    21,192 ms   0.83%\n  strict, linkers only                          19,432 ms   0.765%\n    - Protocol-subcategory, among the 25        15,087 ms   0.594%\n    - FRAMEWORK-subcategory, among the 25        4,216 ms   0.166%   <- the prize\n    - Infrastructure-subcategory, among the 25        0 ms   0%\n\nThe 4.5% was the loose filter on the 8-repo cohort EXCLUDING pretix, which alone\ncarries 90% of cohort pass time. The 4.78% was the hypergumbo self-survey — one\nsmall pure-Python repo. Neither was wrong; neither sized this decision.\n\n10 OF THE 13 Framework-subcategory linkers among the 25 cost ZERO measured ms,\nstructurally: they read framework-pattern-enriched symbols, so they are already\nde-facto framework-gated through their data dependency. Gating them is redundant\nfor cost and purely additive for risk.\n\nTHE DECISIVE ARGUMENT IS NOT COST, IT IS THAT THE CHANGE CANNOT BE VALIDATED\nAGAINST ITS OWN FAILURE MODE. A paired bakeoff differential proves no edges lost\nonly on repos WHERE DETECTION SUCCEEDED. The risk is detection failing on a repo\nthe cohort does not contain — and such a repo yields an empty baseline too, so\nthe differential reads clean. A labelled cohort with ground-truth framework\npresence independent of profile.frameworks does not exist.\n\nALSO SETTLED (details in the ADR): a gated-off linker produces NO AnalysisRun,\nso the recall loss cannot be disclosed with today's machinery — a disclosure\nchannel is a BLOCKING PRECONDITION, not a property of the tree; and\nprerequisite_absent is NOT the landing value for a closed gate (ADR-0056).\n\nCRITERION: four conditions, in the ADR. ZERO of the 25 satisfy it. The best\ncandidate, graphql-resolver, fails the cost bar by 13x AND fails the\n\"demonstrated to work\" bar — it emits 0 edges on apollo-server with the\nframework correctly detected, now filed as WI-dinum. Gating an unproven linker\nwould freeze it behind a gate that hides the evidence of its own defect.\n\nTHREE RE-EVALUATION TRIGGERS, each fireable from ordinary bakeoff output with no\ngating work: T1 cost (Framework-subcategory strict-silent >=2% of a survey's\npass time, or >=60,000 ms on one repo); T2 safety; T3 detection stops being\nmanifest-shallow. Full text in ADR-0055."  # 5c15
